Venetium 0047 - hardware H.264 (DXVA/MFT) on the ANGLE-D3D11 render path, not only D3D9 (generalizes 0041 for the Adreno).
0041 gave HW H.264 only when ANGLE had no D3D11 device and borrowed ANGLE's D3D9 device. With 0045 an Adreno renders via
D3D11, so H.264 would fall to software. The decode device (DXVA2 is D3D9) is independent of the render device: give the
decoder its own IDirect3DDevice9Ex when ANGLE has no D3D9 (CreateOwnD3D9DeviceEx, dynamic Direct3DCreate9Ex), keep the D3D9
output path as-is, and for the D3D11 path open the D3D9 render target's shared surface as a D3D11 texture on ANGLE's device
(OpenSharedResource) wrapped via CreateSharedImageForD3D11Video (zero-copy, same adapter). Drop the 'no D3D11 device' gate
in GpuMojoMediaClientWin on ARM32 so DXVA is offered whenever its per-device DXVA2 probe succeeds; software fallback on
failure. x86/x64 D3D11VideoDecoder unchanged; the Tegra's HW decode (ANGLE's D3D9 device) is untouched. NOT MEASURED - needs
an Adreno that exposes a DXVA2 H.264 decoder (the extended d3dprobe measures that).

